/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (RESEARCH GAP As is evident from the existing literature on students' perceptions of online English learning in higher education, it is prominently observable in the global context. At the same time, there is a limited number of research in the Sri Lankancontext. The existing literature also suggests that no research has been conducted in the Sri Lankan scienceESL undergraduate domainusing the TAM modeland mixed methodology approaches, where online learning initiatives are further limited due to the heightened emphasis on practical learning components within the curriculum. Filling the existing gaps, the current research develops a conceptual inquiry that focuses on English as a Second Language \(ESL\) science undergraduate courses online learning. Its synthesis of the relevant literature narrows the study to the group of science students within the ESL environment, explains the conceptual framework, and adds to the pedagogical discussion of online learning integration into the context of teaching students with ESL as their background. The paper proves that with the proper design of online ESL lectures, the positive effect of the online ESL programs could be maximized on both the instructor and the learner levels, thus enhancing the overall effectiveness of the university online ESL programs.)
/E (RESEARCH GAP As is evident from the existing literature on students' perceptions of online English learning in higher education, it is prominently observable in the global context. At the same time, there is a limited number of research in the Sri Lankancontext. The existing literature also suggests that no research has been conducted in the Sri Lankan scienceESL undergraduate domainusing the TAM modeland mixed methodology approaches, where online learning initiatives are further limited due to the heightened emphasis on practical learning components within the curriculum. Filling the existing gaps, the current research develops a conceptual inquiry that focuses on English as a Second Language \(ESL\) science undergraduate courses online learning. Its synthesis of the relevant literature narrows the study to the group of science students within the ESL environment, explains the conceptual framework, and adds to the pedagogical discussion of online learning integration into the context of teaching students with ESL as their background. The paper proves that with the proper design of online ESL lectures, the positive effect of the online ESL programs could be maximized on both the instructor and the learner levels, thus enhancing the overall effectiveness of the university online ESL programs.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [0 1]
>>
