/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (When considered together, the results highlight that while online learning environments provide unique pedagogical advantages, their effectiveness depends on flexibility, personalization, and commitment to the requirements of learners. The aforementioned research bolsters the increasing need for hybrid models that strike a balance between the social and communicative richness of in-person teaching and technological efficiency. This approach is especially pertinent to English language training in Sri Lankan higher education \(Martin et al., 2020; Dhawan, 2020\).)
